Rem ==================================================================
Rem regex.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: regular expressions
Rem
Rem A pattern is READ ONCE into a compiled program and matched many
Rem times. RxRead parses the pattern to a tree, the tree is compiled to
Rem a small instruction program, and the program is run over a subject
Rem by a virtual machine that advances one code unit at a time and
Rem NEVER BACKTRACKS.
Rem
Rem     Select Case RxRead("([0-9]+)-([0-9]+)", RxNoOpts())
Rem         Case Ok(p)
Rem             RxTest(p, "order 1234-5678 shipped")     Rem True
Rem         Case Err(why, at)
Rem             Print(why & " at " & Str(at))
Rem
Rem NOTHING HERE ABORTS. A malformed pattern is Err(why, at) on the
Rem language's own Result; an absent match or an unset group is None()
Rem on its Option; there is no third outcome and there is not one
Rem call to Error in this file. That is the contract cuttle.shoddy and
Rem reckoner.shoddy hold to, and these words are destined for the same
Rem keyboard: a word that can end a session cannot be seeded.
Rem
Rem THE ENGINE IS A PIKE VM, NOT A BACKTRACKER. Matching cost is
Rem bounded by pattern size times subject length. There is no input
Rem that makes (a|a)*b take exponential time, because there is no
Rem backtracking to be exponential in.
Rem
Rem THE CEILING IS THE PRICE OF THE GUARANTEE. No backreferences and no
Rem lookaround — not "not yet", but the exact things a parallel state
Rem set structurally cannot express. Both are refused BY NAME at their
Rem offset, so a caller learns the ceiling from the tool rather than
Rem from a wrong answer.
Rem
Rem Conventions, all of them load-bearing:
Rem
Rem   * CHR IS NEVER CALLED, AND NEITHER IS ASC. CHR of zero is the empty
Rem     string, so any path that decodes an escape to a code and then
Rem     builds a character with Chr silently loses a NUL. Where this
Rem     machine must turn a code back into text it uses FromCodes,
Rem     which is Codes' exact inverse and admits 0 — which is why the
Rem     \0 and \x00 escapes are ordinary literals in this dialect and
Rem     match a real NUL with no special case at all. The engine
Rem     compares NUMBERS.
Rem
Rem   * EVERY READ OF A CHARACTER IS BOUNDS-CHECKED BY THE CALLER. Nth,
Rem     CodeAt and Asc all abort outside their domain, and Mid clamps
Rem     instead, which puts the abort a word away from the mistake. The
Rem     pattern and the subject are both read through RxUnitAt, which
Rem     answers 0 - 1 outside 1 .. n, and the program is read only after
Rem     a range test on the counter. The two greps tst/regextest.shoddy
Rem     names in its header — for a call to ERROR and for a call to CHR,
Rem     both of which must count zero in this file — are necessary and
Rem     NOT sufficient; THIS is the rest of the totality argument, and no
Rem     grep can check it.
Rem
Rem   * THE CHARACTER DOMAIN IS UTF-16 CODE UNITS, CLASSED AS ASCII.
Rem     Subjects and patterns are indexed by code unit, matching Len,
Rem     Mid, Instr and Codes in the runtime, so a non-BMP character is
Rem     two code units and a dot matches one of them. The digit class is
Rem     0-9; the word class adds A-Z a-z and underscore; the space class
Rem     is tab LF VT FF CR space. Case folding maps A-Z to a-z and
Rem     nothing else — which is exactly what the runtime's own Upper and
Rem     Lower do, so no Turkish-dotless caveat is needed here because no
Rem     such folding is claimed.
Rem
Rem   * LEFTMOST-FIRST, NOT LEFTMOST-LONGEST. Among matches starting at
Rem     the earliest position the answer is the one a backtracker would
Rem     have found first: alternation prefers its left branch, a greedy
Rem     quantifier one more repetition, a lazy one fewer, applied
Rem     outside-in. a|ab against "abc" matches "a". This is Perl's rule,
Rem     not POSIX's, and it is what makes a lazy quantifier mean
Rem     anything at all.
Rem
Rem   * AN UNSET GROUP IS NOT AN EMPTY ONE. RxUnset and RxGot(at, text)
Rem     are different values, because "did not participate" and "matched
Rem     nothing" are different facts. A hit's capture list always has
Rem     exactly RxCount(p) entries, one per capturing group, in order.
Rem
Rem   * THE SIZE CAP IS A REFUSAL, NOT A PAUSE. A counted repetition
Rem     compiles by duplication, so a{100000} would be a hundred
Rem     thousand instructions. RxMaxCode() bounds the program,
Rem     RxMaxPat() the pattern text, RxMaxDepth() the nesting, and each
Rem     refusal names its number.
Rem
Rem   * THE VISITED SET IS WHAT MAKES (a*)* TERMINATE. An epsilon loop
Rem     revisits a program counter it has already reached at this
Rem     position and is cut. It is not an optimisation; without it the
Rem     closure does not terminate.
Rem
Rem Pure throughout: nothing here reads a file, writes one, or prints.
Rem RxDisasm returns lines; it does not print them. NO INCLUDES — every
Rem word this machine needs is a builtin, so its "uses" table is empty
Rem and it drags nothing into a program that reaches for it.
Rem ==================================================================

Rem ---- the code units this file names ---------------------------------
Rem Private to this file: a top-level Let declares a value, not a word,
Rem so nothing here crosses the manifest. Spelling them out is what lets
Rem the parser below read as prose instead of as a table of magic
Rem numbers, and it is why neither Asc nor Chr appears anywhere.

Let rxLf = 10
Let rxBang = 33
Let rxHash = 35
Let rxDollar = 36
Let rxTick = 39
Let rxLpar = 40
Let rxRpar = 41
Let rxStar = 42
Let rxPlus = 43
Let rxComma = 44
Let rxDash = 45
Let rxDot = 46
Let rxZero = 48
Let rxNine = 57
Let rxColon = 58
Let rxLt = 60
Let rxEq = 61
Let rxGt = 62
Let rxQuery = 63
Let rxUpA = 65
Let rxUpZ = 90
Let rxLbrack = 91
Let rxBslash = 92
Let rxRbrack = 93
Let rxCaret = 94
Let rxUnder = 95
Let rxLoA = 97
Let rxLoZ = 122
Let rxLbrace = 123
Let rxPipe = 124
Let rxRbrace = 125

Rem The escape and flag letters, by code, so the dispatches below can
Rem name what they are looking at.

Let rxUcB = 66
Let rxUcD = 68
Let rxUcE = 69
Let rxUcG = 71
Let rxUcN = 78
Let rxUcP = 80
Let rxUcQ = 81
Let rxUcR = 82
Let rxUcS = 83
Let rxUcW = 87
Let rxLcB = 98
Let rxLcC = 99
Let rxLcD = 100
Let rxLcF = 102
Let rxLcI = 105
Let rxLcK = 107
Let rxLcM = 109
Let rxLcN = 110
Let rxLcP = 112
Let rxLcR = 114
Let rxLcS = 115
Let rxLcT = 116
Let rxLcU = 117
Let rxLcV = 118
Let rxLcW = 119
Let rxLcX = 120

Rem ---- what a pattern is asked to do ----------------------------------
Rem Three Booleans, and the compiler bakes all three into the emitted
Rem instructions, so the virtual machine never consults them.

Type RxOpts
    RxFold   As Boolean
    RxDotAll As Boolean
    RxMulti  As Boolean

Rem A run of code units, low and high inclusive. Over NUMBERS and not
Rem over one-character strings: the inner loop compares numbers, and the
Rem subject arrives from Codes already as numbers.

Type RxRange
    RxLo As Number
    RxHi As Number

Rem ---- the parsed pattern ---------------------------------------------
Rem One line, because a sum type spread over several lines is unexpected
Rem indent at top level. RxNil is not optional: concatenation needs an
Rem identity and (?:) has to parse to something. A non-capturing group
Rem parses to its body and leaves no node behind; RxGrp is capturing
Rem only, and carries the number it was given at its opening paren.
Rem Unbounded repetition is spelled as a max of 0 - 1.

Type RxNode = RxNil | RxLit(RxLitCode As Number) | RxCls(RxClsNeg As Boolean, RxClsRanges As List Of RxRange) | RxAny | RxBol | RxEol | RxWb(RxWbNeg As Boolean) | RxCat(RxCatL As RxNode, RxCatR As RxNode) | RxAlt(RxAltL As RxNode, RxAltR As RxNode) | RxRep(RxRepBody As RxNode, RxRepMin As Number, RxRepMax As Number, RxRepLazy As Boolean) | RxGrp(RxGrpBody As RxNode, RxGrpNum As Number)

Rem ---- the compiled program -------------------------------------------
Rem Thompson's instruction set, with absolute targets. Slots 0 and 1 are
Rem the whole match, so capturing group k uses 2k and 2k+1 — the
Rem standard layout, and the reason a hit's capture list can be built by
Rem one pass over the slot array.

Type RxInst = RxIChar(RxICode As Number) | RxICls(RxIClsNeg As Boolean, RxIClsRs As List Of RxRange) | RxIAny(RxIAll As Boolean) | RxISplit(RxISpX As Number, RxISpY As Number) | RxIJmp(RxIJTo As Number) | RxISave(RxISlot As Number) | RxIBol(RxIBMulti As Boolean) | RxIEol(RxIEMulti As Boolean) | RxIWb(RxIWbNeg As Boolean) | RxIMatch

Rem The compiled pattern as a value. The options field is RxHow and not
Rem RxOpts, because a field accessor is an exported global word and the
Rem options record already owns that name.

Type RxProg
    RxSrc  As String
    RxCode As Array Of RxInst
    RxNCap As Number
    RxHow  As RxOpts

Rem ---- what a match answers with --------------------------------------
Rem RxUnset is not RxGot(k, ""). (a)|(b) against "b" leaves group 1
Rem unset and group 2 got, carrying "b"; (a?) against "" leaves group 1
Rem GOT, carrying "". Two different facts, kept different by the type.

Type RxCap = RxUnset | RxGot(RxCapAt As Number, RxCapText As String)

Type RxHit
    RxHitAt   As Number
    RxHitLen  As Number
    RxHitText As String
    RxHitCaps As List Of RxCap

Rem ---- what the parser hands back at each step ------------------------
Rem Nothing is mutable, so the group counter threads through the parse
Rem and comes back alongside the node. RxTkGrp is how many capturing
Rem groups have been opened so far; at the top it is RxCount.

Type RxTake = RxTook(RxTkNode As RxNode, RxTkNext As Number, RxTkGrp As Number) | RxTkBad(RxTkWhy As String, RxTkAt As Number)

Type RxCTake = RxCTook(RxCtRs As List Of RxRange, RxCtNext As Number) | RxCtBad(RxCtWhy As String, RxCtAt As Number)

Type RxQTake = RxQTook(RxQtMin As Number, RxQtMax As Number, RxQtNext As Number) | RxQtBad(RxQtWhy As String, RxQtAt As Number)

Type RxItem = RxItCode(RxItC As Number, RxItNext As Number) | RxItRs(RxItRanges As List Of RxRange, RxItRNext As Number) | RxItBad(RxItWhy As String, RxItAt As Number)

Type RxPre = RxPreOk(RxPrHow As RxOpts, RxPrNext As Number) | RxPreBad(RxPrWhy As String, RxPrAt As Number)

Rem ---- what the virtual machine carries -------------------------------
Rem A thread is a program counter and its own copy of the capture slots.
Rem Threads must not share one array: SetNth clones, so a slot write on
Rem one thread cannot be seen by another, which is the whole reason
Rem (a)|(b) can leave one group unset while the other is got.

Type RxThread
    RxThPc    As Number
    RxThSlots As Array Of Number

Type RxAdds
    RxAdList As List Of RxThread
    RxAdSeen As Array Of Boolean

Type RxStep
    RxStPend As List Of RxThread
    RxStBest As Array Of Number

Rem ---- the classes the shorthands stand for ---------------------------
Rem Written out rather than complemented at run time, so \D \W and \S
Rem contribute ranges inside a class exactly as \d \w and \s do, with no
Rem negation machinery in the class parser at all.

Let rxDigitRs = { RxRange(48, 57) }
Let rxNotDigitRs = { RxRange(0, 47), RxRange(58, 65535) }
Let rxWordRs = { RxRange(48, 57), RxRange(65, 90), RxRange(95, 95), RxRange(97, 122) }
Let rxNotWordRs = { RxRange(0, 47), RxRange(58, 64), RxRange(91, 94), RxRange(96, 96), RxRange(123, 65535) }
Let rxSpaceRs = { RxRange(9, 13), RxRange(32, 32) }
Let rxNotSpaceRs = { RxRange(0, 8), RxRange(14, 31), RxRange(33, 65535) }

Rem ---- the ceilings, each named in the refusal that cites it ----------
Rem Zero-arg Defs and not top-level Lets, because these DO cross the
Rem manifest: a caller and a suite both want to ask what the limit is.

Rem The compiled program's instruction count. Past this a counted
Rem repetition is refused at parse time rather than built and crawled
Rem through.
Rem
Rem CHOSEN AGAINST Ticks, AND THE MEASUREMENTS ARE WORTH WRITING DOWN
Rem because the shape of the cost is not what a reader expects:
Rem
Rem     28 instructions over 2000 characters      25 ms
Rem     204 instructions over 1000 characters    693 ms
Rem     1994 instructions over 1000 characters  3114 ms
Rem
Rem So the ceiling is not a cliff, it is a slope, and the cap sits where
Rem a pattern nobody would write by hand meets a wait nobody would sit
Rem through. The first line is the real case — an ordinary pattern over
Rem an ordinary subject — and it is what the machine is for. The last is
Rem a{1990}b, which is the cap doing its job by never being reached.
Def RxMaxCode() As Number
    2000

Rem The pattern text, in code units. Separate from RxMaxCode because a
Rem pattern can be long and compile to nothing — (?:) repeated is four
Rem characters and no instructions — and because bounding the text is
Rem what bounds the parser's own recursion.
Def RxMaxPat() As Number
    2000

Rem How deeply groups and alternations may nest. The grammar below is
Rem mutual recursion, which costs stack in this runtime, so the depth is
Rem refused rather than discovered.
Def RxMaxDepth() As Number
    100

Rem ---- reading a character, once, in one place ------------------------
Rem THE WHOLE BOUNDS DISCIPLINE IS HERE. Nth aborts outside 1 .. n, so
Rem every read of the pattern and of the subject goes through this word,
Rem which answers 0 - 1 instead. A code unit is 0 .. 65535, so 0 - 1 is
Rem a value no character can have and no comparison below can match by
Rem accident. Mid is deliberately not used for this: Mid CLAMPS, which
Rem would hand back a real character for a position past the end.

Def RxUnitAt(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number) As Number
    If k < 1 Or k > n Then
        0 - 1
    Else
        Nth(cs, k)

Rem ---- the ASCII classes, stated once ---------------------------------

Def RxIsDigitC(c As Number) As Boolean
    c >= rxZero And c <= rxNine

Def RxIsAlpha(c As Number) As Boolean
    (c >= rxUpA And c <= rxUpZ) Or (c >= rxLoA And c <= rxLoZ)

Def RxIsAlnum(c As Number) As Boolean
    RxIsDigitC(c) Or RxIsAlpha(c)

Def RxIsWordCh(c As Number) As Boolean
    RxIsAlnum(c) Or c = rxUnder

Def RxHexVal(c As Number) As Number
    If RxIsDigitC(c) Then
        c - rxZero
    Else
        If c >= rxLoA And c <= rxLoA + 5 Then
            c - rxLoA + 10
        Else
            If c >= rxUpA And c <= rxUpA + 5 Then
                c - rxUpA + 10
            Else
                0 - 1

Rem The metacharacters, which is exactly the set RxQuote escapes.

Def RxIsMeta(c As Number) As Boolean
    c = rxDot Or c = rxStar Or c = rxPlus Or c = rxQuery Or c = rxLpar Or c = rxRpar Or c = rxLbrack Or c = rxRbrack Or c = rxLbrace Or c = rxRbrace Or c = rxPipe Or c = rxCaret Or c = rxDollar Or c = rxBslash Or c = rxDash

Rem The class shorthands, and the ranges each stands for.

Def RxIsShort(c As Number) As Boolean
    c = rxLcD Or c = rxUcD Or c = rxLcW Or c = rxUcW Or c = rxLcS Or c = rxUcS

Def RxShortRs(c As Number) As List Of RxRange
    Select Case c
        Case 100
            rxDigitRs
        Case 68
            rxNotDigitRs
        Case 119
            rxWordRs
        Case 87
            rxNotWordRs
        Case 115
            rxSpaceRs
        Case Else
            rxNotSpaceRs

Rem The control escapes. Note \0 answers 0 and 0 is a real code unit, so
Rem the test at every call site is "is this at least 0", never "is this
Rem true" — a NUL is not an absence here.

Def RxCtrlCode(c As Number) As Number
    Select Case c
        Case 110
            10
        Case 116
            9
        Case 114
            13
        Case 102
            12
        Case 118
            11
        Case 48
            0
        Case Else
            0 - 1

Rem ---- the constructs refused BY NAME ---------------------------------
Rem A pattern that silently means something other than what it says is
Rem the failure mode this machine exists to avoid, so every one of these
Rem is named where it is written rather than reported as an unexpected
Rem character. Answering "" means "not one of these".

Def RxRefused(c As Number) As String
    Select Case c
        Case 49 To 57
            "REGEX: BACKREFERENCES ARE NOT SUPPORTED — THE ENGINE DOES NOT BACKTRACK"
        Case 107
            "REGEX: NAMED BACKREFERENCES ARE NOT SUPPORTED — THE ENGINE DOES NOT BACKTRACK"
        Case 112, 80
            "REGEX: UNICODE PROPERTIES ARE NOT SUPPORTED — THE DOMAIN IS UTF-16 CODE UNITS CLASSED AS ASCII"
        Case 65
            "REGEX: " & RxBs() & "A IS NOT SUPPORTED — WRITE ^ FOR THE START OF THE SUBJECT"
        Case 122, 90
            "REGEX: " & RxBs() & "z AND " & RxBs() & "Z ARE NOT SUPPORTED — WRITE $ FOR THE END OF THE SUBJECT"
        Case 71
            "REGEX: " & RxBs() & "G IS NOT SUPPORTED — THERE IS NO CARRIED MATCH ANCHOR"
        Case 81, 69
            "REGEX: " & RxBs() & "Q AND " & RxBs() & "E QUOTING IS NOT SUPPORTED — RxQuote ESCAPES A STRING INSTEAD"
        Case 82
            "REGEX: " & RxBs() & "R IS NOT SUPPORTED"
        Case 78
            "REGEX: " & RxBs() & "N IS NOT SUPPORTED"
        Case 117
            "REGEX: " & RxBs() & "u IS NOT SUPPORTED — A CODE UNIT BELOW 256 IS WRITTEN " & RxBs() & "xHH"
        Case 99
            "REGEX: " & RxBs() & "cX CONTROL ESCAPES ARE NOT SUPPORTED"
        Case Else
            ""

Rem One backslash, as a string. Written once so no message below has to
Rem carry a doubled backslash and be misread as two.
Def RxBs() As String
    "\\"

Rem ---- the options ----------------------------------------------------

Rem Nothing on: the dot stops at a newline, ^ and $ are the ends of the
Rem whole subject, and case is compared exactly.
Def RxNoOpts() As RxOpts
    RxOpts(False, False, False)

Rem ASCII case folding on, and nothing else.
Def RxFoldOpts() As RxOpts
    RxOpts(True, False, False)

Rem ---- reading a pattern ----------------------------------------------
Rem THE ONLY WORD IN THIS MACHINE THAT CAN FAIL, and the only Result in
Rem it. Every match word below takes a compiled program, which can only
Rem have come from an Ok — so they are total by construction, because
Rem there is no argument left that can be wrong.

Def RxRead(pat As String, how As RxOpts) As Result
    If Len(pat) > RxMaxPat() Then
        Err("REGEX: THE PATTERN IS " & Str(Len(pat)) & " CHARACTERS AND THE LIMIT IS " & Str(RxMaxPat()), 0)
    Else
        RxReadPre(pat, Codes(pat), Len(pat), how)

Def RxReadPre(pat As String, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts) As Result
    Select Case RxPrefix(cs, n, how)
        Case RxPreBad(w, a)
            Err(w, a)
        Case RxPreOk(h2, k0)
            RxReadBody(pat, cs, n, h2, k0)
        Case Else
            Err("REGEX: THE PATTERN COULD NOT BE READ", 0)

Def RxReadBody(pat As String, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, k0 As Number) As Result
    Select Case RxPAlt(cs, n, k0, 0, 0, how)
        Case RxTkBad(w, a)
            Err(w, a)
        Case RxTook(t, k2, g2)
            If k2 <= n Then
                RxReadLeft(cs, n, k2)
            Else
                RxBuild(pat, t, g2, how)
        Case Else
            Err("REGEX: THE PATTERN COULD NOT BE READ", 0)

Rem The grammar stops at a ) it cannot account for and at nothing else,
Rem so text left over means exactly one thing.
Def RxReadLeft(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k2 As Number) As Result
    If RxUnitAt(cs, n, k2) = rxRpar Then
        Err("REGEX: UNMATCHED ) — THERE IS NO GROUP OPEN HERE", k2)
    Else
        Err("REGEX: THE PATTERN DID NOT READ TO ITS END", k2)

Rem ---- the flag prefix, stripped before the grammar runs --------------
Rem (?i) (?s) (?m) and their combinations, at offset 1 and nowhere else.
Rem Written as a tiny reader in front of the grammar so the grammar
Rem itself stays flag-free, and refused BY NAME anywhere later.
Rem
Rem WHERE BOTH ARE GIVEN THE PREFIX WINS, WHOLE. A prefix does not merge
Rem with the options argument, it replaces it: (?i) on a pattern read
Rem with RxOpts(False, True, False) is folding ON and dot-all OFF. The
Rem pattern is closer to the intent than the call site, and a rule that
Rem replaces is one a caller can state; a rule that merges is one they
Rem have to work out.

Rem The guard is the whole of what makes this reader safe to put in
Rem front of the grammar: it claims the text ONLY when it is (? then
Rem flag letters then ), so (?: and (?= and (?i: all fall through
Rem untouched and are refused by name where they are written.
Def RxPrefix(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts) As RxPre
    If RxUnitAt(cs, n, 1) = rxLpar And RxUnitAt(cs, n, 2) = rxQuery And RxIsFlagCh(RxUnitAt(cs, n, 3)) And RxUnitAt(cs, n, RxFlagEnd(cs, n, 3)) = rxRpar Then
        RxPrefixScan(cs, n, 3, False, False, False)
    Else
        RxPreOk(how, 1)

Def RxIsFlagCh(c As Number) As Boolean
    c = rxLcI Or c = rxLcS Or c = rxLcM Or c = rxLcX

Def RxPrefixScan(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, i As Number, f As Boolean, s As Boolean, m As Boolean) As RxPre
    Let c = RxUnitAt(cs, n, i)
    If c = rxLcI Then
        RxPrefixScan(cs, n, i + 1, True, s, m)
    Else
        If c = rxLcS Then
            RxPrefixScan(cs, n, i + 1, f, True, m)
        Else
            If c = rxLcM Then
                RxPrefixScan(cs, n, i + 1, f, s, True)
            Else
                If c = rxLcX Then
                    RxPreBad("REGEX: THE x FLAG IS NOT SUPPORTED — THERE IS NO WHITESPACE-INSENSITIVE MODE", i)
                Else
                    If c = rxRpar Then
                        RxPreOk(RxOpts(f, s, m), i + 1)
                    Else
                        RxPreBad("REGEX: A FLAG GROUP MAY ONLY CONTAIN i, s AND m", i)

Rem ==================================================================
Rem THE PARSER
Rem
Rem Recursive descent over a 1-based offset, the shape alg.shoddy and
Rem json.shoddy already use. Precedence, lowest first:
Rem
Rem     alt   := cat ( "|" cat )*
Rem     cat   := rep*
Rem     rep   := atom ( "*" | "+" | "?" | "{" ... "}" ) "?"?
Rem     atom  := "(" ( "?:" )? alt ")" | "[" class "]" | "." | "^" | "$"
Rem            | escape | literal
Rem
Rem GROUP NUMBERING IS BY OPENING PAREN, LEFT TO RIGHT, assigned as the
Rem parser descends — so ((a)(b)) numbers the outer 1. A compiler that
Rem numbered as it emitted would get that wrong the moment an
Rem alternation reordered emission.
Rem ==================================================================

Rem Alternation is right-nested, so a|b|c is RxAlt(a, RxAlt(b, c)) and
Rem the left branch is always the higher priority — which is leftmost-
Rem first, spelled in the tree.
Def RxPAlt(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts) As RxTake
    If d > RxMaxDepth() Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: THE PATTERN NESTS MORE THAN " & Str(RxMaxDepth()) & " DEEP", k)
    Else
        RxPAltGo(cs, n, k, g, d, how)

Def RxPAltGo(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts) As RxTake
    Select Case RxPCat(cs, n, k, g, d, how)
        Case RxTkBad(w, a)
            RxTkBad(w, a)
        Case RxTook(l, k2, g2)
            If RxUnitAt(cs, n, k2) = rxPipe Then
                RxPAltMore(cs, n, k2, g2, d, how, l)
            Else
                RxTook(l, k2, g2)
        Case Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: THE PATTERN COULD NOT BE READ", k)

Def RxPAltMore(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts, l As RxNode) As RxTake
    Select Case RxPAlt(cs, n, k + 1, g, d + 1, how)
        Case RxTkBad(w, a)
            RxTkBad(w, a)
        Case RxTook(r, k3, g3)
            RxTook(RxAlt(l, r), k3, g3)
        Case Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: THE PATTERN COULD NOT BE READ", k)

Rem Concatenation runs until | or ) or the end of the pattern.
Def RxPCat(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts) As RxTake
    RxPCatGo(cs, n, k, g, d, how, RxNil())

Def RxPCatGo(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts, acc As RxNode) As RxTake
    Let c = RxUnitAt(cs, n, k)
    If c = 0 - 1 Or c = rxPipe Or c = rxRpar Then
        RxTook(acc, k, g)
    Else
        If RxIsQuantCh(c) Then
            RxPNothing(c, k)
        Else
            RxPCatStep(cs, n, k, g, d, how, acc)

Rem A quantifier at the START of a term has nothing in front of it. This
Rem is where *abc and a** and {2}x are caught, and where a brace that
Rem was meant literally is told what to write instead.
Def RxIsQuantCh(c As Number) As Boolean
    c = rxStar Or c = rxPlus Or c = rxQuery Or c = rxLbrace

Def RxPNothing(c As Number, k As Number) As RxTake
    If c = rxLbrace Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: NOTHING TO REPEAT — WRITE " & RxBs() & "{ FOR A LITERAL BRACE", k)
    Else
        RxTkBad("REGEX: NOTHING TO REPEAT", k)

Def RxPCatStep(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts, acc As RxNode) As RxTake
    Select Case RxPRep(cs, n, k, g, d, how)
        Case RxTkBad(w, a)
            RxTkBad(w, a)
        Case RxTook(t, k2, g2)
            RxPCatGo(cs, n, k2, g2, d, how, RxCatOf(acc, t))
        Case Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: THE PATTERN COULD NOT BE READ", k)

Rem One atom, then at most one quantifier, then at most one lazy mark.
Def RxPRep(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts) As RxTake
    Select Case RxPAtom(cs, n, k, g, d, how)
        Case RxTkBad(w, a)
            RxTkBad(w, a)
        Case RxTook(t, k2, g2)
            RxPQuant(cs, n, k2, g2, t)
        Case Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: THE PATTERN COULD NOT BE READ", k)

Def RxPQuant(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, t As RxNode) As RxTake
    Let c = RxUnitAt(cs, n, k)
    If c = rxStar Then
        RxPLazy(cs, n, k + 1, g, t, 0, 0 - 1)
    Else
        If c = rxPlus Then
            RxPLazy(cs, n, k + 1, g, t, 1, 0 - 1)
        Else
            If c = rxQuery Then
                RxPLazy(cs, n, k + 1, g, t, 0, 1)
            Else
                If c = rxLbrace Then
                    RxPCounted(cs, n, k, g, t)
                Else
                    RxTook(t, k, g)

Rem A ? after a quantifier makes it lazy; a + after one would make it
Rem possessive, which needs the engine to refuse to give ground it has
Rem taken — and there is no ground taken to give back here.
Def RxPLazy(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, t As RxNode, lo As Number, hi As Number) As RxTake
    Let c = RxUnitAt(cs, n, k)
    If c = rxPlus Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: POSSESSIVE QUANTIFIERS ARE NOT SUPPORTED — THE ENGINE DOES NOT BACKTRACK", k)
    Else
        If c = rxQuery Then
            RxTook(RxRep(t, lo, hi, True), k + 1, g)
        Else
            RxTook(RxRep(t, lo, hi, False), k, g)

Rem ---- counted repetition, and the size cap ---------------------------
Rem A counted repetition compiles by duplication, so the refusal has to
Rem happen HERE, at parse time, with the offset of the brace and the
Rem number named — not after building a program the machine would then
Rem crawl through.

Def RxPCounted(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, t As RxNode) As RxTake
    Select Case RxPBraces(cs, n, k)
        Case RxQtBad(w, a)
            RxTkBad(w, a)
        Case RxQTook(lo, hi, k2)
            RxPCountCap(cs, n, k, k2, g, t, lo, hi)
        Case Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: THE COUNTED REPETITION COULD NOT BE READ", k)

Def RxPCountCap(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, k2 As Number, g As Number, t As RxNode, lo As Number, hi As Number) As RxTake
    Let need = RxRepSize(RxSize(t), lo, hi)
    If need > RxMaxCode() Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: " & RxBraceText(lo, hi) & " IS TOO MANY REPETITIONS — IT WOULD COMPILE TO " & Str(need) & " INSTRUCTIONS AND THE LIMIT IS " & Str(RxMaxCode()), k)
    Else
        If RxUnitAt(cs, n, k2) = rxQuery Then
            RxTook(RxRep(t, lo, hi, True), k2 + 1, g)
        Else
            RxTook(RxRep(t, lo, hi, False), k2, g)

Def RxBraceText(lo As Number, hi As Number) As String
    If hi = 0 - 1 Then
        "{" & Str(lo) & ",}"
    Else
        If hi = lo Then
            "{" & Str(lo) & "}"
        Else
            "{" & Str(lo) & "," & Str(hi) & "}"

Rem {m} {m,} {m,n}, starting at the brace.
Def RxPBraces(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number) As RxQTake
    Let e1 = RxDigitEnd(cs, n, k + 1)
    If e1 = k + 1 Then
        RxQtBad("REGEX: A COUNTED REPETITION NEEDS A NUMBER — WRITE {2}, {2,} OR {2,5}", k)
    Else
        RxPBraces2(cs, n, k, e1, RxNumAt(cs, n, k + 1, e1, 0))

Def RxPBraces2(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, e1 As Number, lo As Number) As RxQTake
    Let c = RxUnitAt(cs, n, e1)
    If c = rxRbrace Then
        RxQTook(lo, lo, e1 + 1)
    Else
        If c = rxComma Then
            RxPBraces3(cs, n, k, e1, lo)
        Else
            RxQtBad("REGEX: UNTERMINATED { — A COUNTED REPETITION NEEDS A CLOSING }", k)

Def RxPBraces3(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, e1 As Number, lo As Number) As RxQTake
    Let e2 = RxDigitEnd(cs, n, e1 + 1)
    If e2 = e1 + 1 Then
        If RxUnitAt(cs, n, e2) = rxRbrace Then
            RxQTook(lo, 0 - 1, e2 + 1)
        Else
            RxQtBad("REGEX: UNTERMINATED { — A COUNTED REPETITION NEEDS A CLOSING }", k)
    Else
        RxPBraces4(cs, n, k, e2, lo, RxNumAt(cs, n, e1 + 1, e2, 0))

Def RxPBraces4(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, e2 As Number, lo As Number, hi As Number) As RxQTake
    If RxUnitAt(cs, n, e2) <> rxRbrace Then
        RxQtBad("REGEX: UNTERMINATED { — A COUNTED REPETITION NEEDS A CLOSING }", k)
    Else
        If hi < lo Then
            RxQtBad("REGEX: " & RxBraceText(lo, hi) & " IS BACKWARDS — THE LOW COUNT MUST NOT EXCEED THE HIGH", k)
        Else
            RxQTook(lo, hi, e2 + 1)

Def RxDigitEnd(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, i As Number) As Number
    If RxIsDigitC(RxUnitAt(cs, n, i)) Then
        RxDigitEnd(cs, n, i + 1)
    Else
        i

Def RxNumAt(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, i As Number, j As Number, acc As Number) As Number
    If i >= j Then
        acc
    Else
        RxNumAt(cs, n, i + 1, j, acc * 10 + (RxUnitAt(cs, n, i) - rxZero))

Rem ---- one atom -------------------------------------------------------

Def RxPAtom(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts) As RxTake
    If d > RxMaxDepth() Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: THE PATTERN NESTS MORE THAN " & Str(RxMaxDepth()) & " DEEP", k)
    Else
        RxPAtomAt(cs, n, k, g, d, how, RxUnitAt(cs, n, k))

Def RxPAtomAt(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts, c As Number) As RxTake
    If c = 0 - 1 Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: THE PATTERN ENDS WHERE SOMETHING TO MATCH WAS EXPECTED", k)
    Else
        If c = rxLpar Then
            RxPGroup(cs, n, k, g, d, how)
        Else
            If c = rxLbrack Then
                RxPClass(cs, n, k, g)
            Else
                If c = rxDot Then
                    RxTook(RxAny(), k + 1, g)
                Else
                    If c = rxCaret Then
                        RxTook(RxBol(), k + 1, g)
                    Else
                        If c = rxDollar Then
                            RxTook(RxEol(), k + 1, g)
                        Else
                            If c = rxBslash Then
                                RxPEscape(cs, n, k, g)
                            Else
                                RxTook(RxLit(c), k + 1, g)

Rem ---- groups ---------------------------------------------------------

Def RxPGroup(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts) As RxTake
    If RxUnitAt(cs, n, k + 1) = rxQuery Then
        RxPGroupQ(cs, n, k, g, d, how, RxUnitAt(cs, n, k + 2))
    Else
        RxPGroupCap(cs, n, k, g + 1, d, how)

Rem The number is this group's, taken at the opening paren and BEFORE
Rem descending, so an inner group can only be given a higher one.
Def RxPGroupCap(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, gn As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts) As RxTake
    Select Case RxPAlt(cs, n, k + 1, gn, d + 1, how)
        Case RxTkBad(w, a)
            RxTkBad(w, a)
        Case RxTook(b, k2, g2)
            If RxUnitAt(cs, n, k2) = rxRpar Then
                RxTook(RxGrp(b, gn), k2 + 1, g2)
            Else
                RxTkBad("REGEX: UNMATCHED ( — THIS GROUP NEVER CLOSES", k)
        Case Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: THE GROUP COULD NOT BE READ", k)

Rem A non-capturing group parses to its body and leaves no node behind.
Def RxPGroupPlain(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts) As RxTake
    Select Case RxPAlt(cs, n, k + 3, g, d + 1, how)
        Case RxTkBad(w, a)
            RxTkBad(w, a)
        Case RxTook(b, k2, g2)
            If RxUnitAt(cs, n, k2) = rxRpar Then
                RxTook(b, k2 + 1, g2)
            Else
                RxTkBad("REGEX: UNMATCHED ( — THIS GROUP NEVER CLOSES", k)
        Case Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: THE GROUP COULD NOT BE READ", k)

Rem Everything (? can open, and what this dialect says about each one.
Rem The point of naming them is that a caller learns the ceiling from
Rem the tool instead of from a wrong answer three words later.
Def RxPGroupQ(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, d As Number, how As RxOpts, c As Number) As RxTake
    If c = rxColon Then
        RxPGroupPlain(cs, n, k, g, d, how)
    Else
        If c = rxEq Then
            RxTkBad("REGEX: LOOKAHEAD IS NOT SUPPORTED — A PARALLEL STATE SET CANNOT LOOK AHEAD", k)
        Else
            If c = rxBang Then
                RxTkBad("REGEX: NEGATIVE LOOKAHEAD IS NOT SUPPORTED — A PARALLEL STATE SET CANNOT LOOK AHEAD", k)
            Else
                If c = rxLt Then
                    RxPGroupLt(cs, n, k, RxUnitAt(cs, n, k + 3))
                Else
                    RxPGroupQ2(cs, n, k, c)

Def RxPGroupLt(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, c4 As Number) As RxTake
    If c4 = rxEq Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: LOOKBEHIND IS NOT SUPPORTED — THE ENGINE READS FORWARD ONLY", k)
    Else
        If c4 = rxBang Then
            RxTkBad("REGEX: NEGATIVE LOOKBEHIND IS NOT SUPPORTED — THE ENGINE READS FORWARD ONLY", k)
        Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: NAMED GROUPS ARE NOT SUPPORTED — GROUPS ARE NUMBERED BY OPENING PAREN", k)

Def RxPGroupQ2(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, c As Number) As RxTake
    If c = rxTick Or c = rxUcP Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: NAMED GROUPS ARE NOT SUPPORTED — GROUPS ARE NUMBERED BY OPENING PAREN", k)
    Else
        If c = rxGt Then
            RxTkBad("REGEX: ATOMIC GROUPS ARE NOT SUPPORTED — THERE IS NO BACKTRACKING TO FORBID", k)
        Else
            If c = rxHash Then
                RxTkBad("REGEX: COMMENT GROUPS ARE NOT SUPPORTED", k)
            Else
                If c = rxLpar Then
                    RxTkBad("REGEX: CONDITIONALS ARE NOT SUPPORTED", k)
                Else
                    If c = rxUcR Or RxIsDigitC(c) Then
                        RxTkBad("REGEX: RECURSION AND SUBROUTINE CALLS ARE NOT SUPPORTED", k)
                    Else
                        RxPGroupQ3(cs, n, k, c)

Rem Flag letters here mean the pattern put (?i) somewhere other than the
Rem front. Which of the two refusals it gets depends on what closes it,
Rem because a scoped flag group and a misplaced one are different
Rem mistakes and deserve different sentences.
Def RxPGroupQ3(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, c As Number) As RxTake
    If Not RxIsFlagCh(c) Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: (? DOES NOT OPEN ANYTHING THIS DIALECT KNOWS", k)
    Else
        RxPGroupQ4(k, RxUnitAt(cs, n, RxFlagEnd(cs, n, k + 2)))

Rem What closes the flag letters says which mistake this is, and the
Rem three are worth different sentences: a scoped flag group asks for
Rem something the compiler does not do, a closed one is in the wrong
Rem place, and anything else is not a flag group at all.
Def RxPGroupQ4(k As Number, term As Number) As RxTake
    If term = rxColon Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: SCOPED INLINE FLAGS ARE NOT SUPPORTED — FLAGS GO AT THE FRONT OF THE WHOLE PATTERN", k)
    Else
        If term = rxRpar Then
            RxTkBad("REGEX: INLINE FLAGS ARE ONLY ALLOWED AT THE START OF A PATTERN", k)
        Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: A FLAG GROUP MAY ONLY CONTAIN i, s AND m", k)

Def RxFlagEnd(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, i As Number) As Number
    If RxIsFlagCh(RxUnitAt(cs, n, i)) Then
        RxFlagEnd(cs, n, i + 1)
    Else
        i

Rem ---- escapes outside a class ----------------------------------------

Def RxPEscape(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number) As RxTake
    RxPEsc1(cs, n, k, g, RxUnitAt(cs, n, k + 1))

Def RxPEsc1(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, c As Number) As RxTake
    If c = 0 - 1 Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: A PATTERN MAY NOT END WITH A BACKSLASH", k)
    Else
        If RxIsShort(c) Then
            RxTook(RxCls(False, RxShortRs(c)), k + 2, g)
        Else
            If c = rxLcB Then
                RxTook(RxWb(False), k + 2, g)
            Else
                If c = rxUcB Then
                    RxTook(RxWb(True), k + 2, g)
                Else
                    If c = rxLcX Then
                        RxPEscHex(cs, n, k, g)
                    Else
                        RxPEsc2(cs, n, k, g, c)

Def RxPEscHex(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number) As RxTake
    Let h1 = RxHexVal(RxUnitAt(cs, n, k + 2))
    Let h2 = RxHexVal(RxUnitAt(cs, n, k + 3))
    If h1 < 0 Or h2 < 0 Then
        RxTkBad("REGEX: " & RxBs() & "x NEEDS TWO HEX DIGITS", k)
    Else
        RxTook(RxLit(16 * h1 + h2), k + 4, g)

Rem \0 answers a code of 0 and 0 is a real code unit, which is why the
Rem test is "at least 0" and not "is true". FromCodes can build a NUL,
Rem so a NUL is an ordinary literal here and matches like any other.
Def RxPEsc2(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, c As Number) As RxTake
    Let v = RxCtrlCode(c)
    If v >= 0 Then
        RxTook(RxLit(v), k + 2, g)
    Else
        If RxRefused(c) <> "" Then
            RxTkBad(RxRefused(c), k)
        Else
            If RxIsAlnum(c) Then
                RxTkBad("REGEX: " & RxBs() & FromCodes({ c }) & " IS NOT AN ESCAPE THIS DIALECT KNOWS", k)
            Else
                RxTook(RxLit(c), k + 2, g)

Rem ---- character classes ----------------------------------------------
Rem Where the fiddly rules live: ] first is a literal ], - first or last
Rem is a literal -, a shorthand inside contributes its ranges, and a
Rem backwards range is refused at the offset of the dash.

Def RxPClass(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number) As RxTake
    RxPClass2(cs, n, k, g, RxUnitAt(cs, n, k + 1) = rxCaret)

Def RxPClass2(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, neg As Boolean) As RxTake
    If neg Then
        RxPClass3(cs, n, k, g, neg, k + 2)
    Else
        RxPClass3(cs, n, k, g, neg, k + 1)

Def RxPClass3(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, neg As Boolean, i As Number) As RxTake
    If RxUnitAt(cs, n, i) = rxRbrack Then
        RxPClassEnd(cs, n, k, g, neg, RxClsGo(cs, n, k, i + 1, { RxRange(93, 93) }))
    Else
        RxPClassEnd(cs, n, k, g, neg, RxClsGo(cs, n, k, i, { }))

Def RxPClassEnd(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, g As Number, neg As Boolean, r As RxCTake) As RxTake
    Select Case r
        Case RxCtBad(w, a)
            RxTkBad(w, a)
        Case RxCTook(rs, k2)
            RxTook(RxCls(neg, rs), k2, g)
        Case Else
            RxTkBad("REGEX: THE CHARACTER CLASS COULD NOT BE READ", k)

Def RxClsGo(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, i As Number, acc As List Of RxRange) As RxCTake
    Let c = RxUnitAt(cs, n, i)
    If c = 0 - 1 Then
        RxCtBad("REGEX: UNTERMINATED [ — A CHARACTER CLASS NEEDS A CLOSING ]", k)
    Else
        If c = rxRbrack Then
            RxCTook(acc, i + 1)
        Else
            If c = rxLbrack And RxUnitAt(cs, n, i + 1) = rxColon Then
                RxCtBad("REGEX: POSIX CHARACTER CLASSES ARE NOT SUPPORTED", i)
            Else
                RxClsItem1(cs, n, k, i, acc, RxClsItem(cs, n, i))

Def RxClsItem1(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, i As Number, acc As List Of RxRange, it As RxItem) As RxCTake
    Select Case it
        Case RxItBad(w, a)
            RxCtBad(w, a)
        Case RxItRs(rs, j)
            RxClsGo(cs, n, k, j, Concat(acc, rs))
        Case RxItCode(c1, j)
            RxClsDash(cs, n, k, acc, c1, j)
        Case Else
            RxCtBad("REGEX: THE CHARACTER CLASS COULD NOT BE READ", i)

Rem A dash that is neither first nor last opens a range; anywhere else
Rem it is an ordinary character, which is why [a-] and [-a] both read.
Def RxClsDash(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, acc As List Of RxRange, c1 As Number, j As Number) As RxCTake
    If RxUnitAt(cs, n, j) = rxDash And RxUnitAt(cs, n, j + 1) <> rxRbrack And RxUnitAt(cs, n, j + 1) <> 0 - 1 Then
        RxClsRange(cs, n, k, acc, c1, j, RxClsItem(cs, n, j + 1))
    Else
        RxClsGo(cs, n, k, j, Concat(acc, { RxRange(c1, c1) }))

Def RxClsRange(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, acc As List Of RxRange, c1 As Number, j As Number, it As RxItem) As RxCTake
    Select Case it
        Case RxItBad(w, a)
            RxCtBad(w, a)
        Case RxItRs(rs, j2)
            RxCtBad("REGEX: A CLASS SHORTHAND CANNOT BE THE FAR END OF A RANGE", j + 1)
        Case RxItCode(c2, j2)
            If c2 < c1 Then
                RxCtBad("REGEX: THE RANGE IS BACKWARDS — THE LOW END MUST NOT EXCEED THE HIGH", j)
            Else
                RxClsGo(cs, n, k, j2, Concat(acc, { RxRange(c1, c2) }))
        Case Else
            RxCtBad("REGEX: THE CHARACTER CLASS COULD NOT BE READ", j)

Def RxClsItem(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, i As Number) As RxItem
    If RxUnitAt(cs, n, i) = rxBslash Then
        RxClsEsc(cs, n, i, RxUnitAt(cs, n, i + 1))
    Else
        RxItCode(RxUnitAt(cs, n, i), i + 1)

Def RxClsEsc(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, i As Number, c As Number) As RxItem
    If c = 0 - 1 Then
        RxItBad("REGEX: A PATTERN MAY NOT END WITH A BACKSLASH", i)
    Else
        If RxIsShort(c) Then
            RxItRs(RxShortRs(c), i + 2)
        Else
            If c = rxLcX Then
                RxClsHex(cs, n, i)
            Else
                RxClsEsc2(cs, n, i, c)

Def RxClsHex(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, i As Number) As RxItem
    Let h1 = RxHexVal(RxUnitAt(cs, n, i + 2))
    Let h2 = RxHexVal(RxUnitAt(cs, n, i + 3))
    If h1 < 0 Or h2 < 0 Then
        RxItBad("REGEX: " & RxBs() & "x NEEDS TWO HEX DIGITS", i)
    Else
        RxItCode(16 * h1 + h2, i + 4)

Rem \b inside a class means a backspace in some dialects and a word
Rem boundary in none of them. Two meanings for one spelling is exactly
Rem what this machine refuses to have, so it is named and refused.
Def RxClsEsc2(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, i As Number, c As Number) As RxItem
    Let v = RxCtrlCode(c)
    If v >= 0 Then
        RxItCode(v, i + 2)
    Else
        If c = rxLcB Or c = rxUcB Then
            RxItBad("REGEX: " & RxBs() & "b IS A WORD BOUNDARY AND HAS NO MEANING INSIDE A CLASS", i)
        Else
            If RxRefused(c) <> "" Then
                RxItBad(RxRefused(c), i)
            Else
                If RxIsAlnum(c) Then
                    RxItBad("REGEX: " & RxBs() & FromCodes({ c }) & " IS NOT AN ESCAPE THIS DIALECT KNOWS", i)
                Else
                    RxItCode(c, i + 2)

Rem ==================================================================
Rem THE COMPILER
Rem
Rem Thompson's construction, emitted with ABSOLUTE JUMP TARGETS COMPUTED
Rem FROM LENGTHS. A two-pass "emit then patch" would need a SetNth per
Rem patch, and SetNth clones the whole sequence; asking each node how
Rem long it is costs nothing and is what makes the emit one pass.
Rem
Rem RxSize is therefore load-bearing twice over: it places every jump,
Rem and it is what lets a counted repetition be refused BEFORE it is
Rem built, by arithmetic on a tree that has not been expanded.
Rem ==================================================================

Def RxSize(t As RxNode) As Number
    Select Case t
        Case RxNil
            0
        Case RxCat(l, r)
            RxSize(l) + RxSize(r)
        Case RxAlt(l, r)
            RxSize(l) + RxSize(r) + 2
        Case RxGrp(b, gn)
            RxSize(b) + 2
        Case RxRep(b, lo, hi, lz)
            RxRepSize(RxSize(b), lo, hi)
        Case Else
            1

Rem What a repetition costs, without expanding it. Unbounded from zero
Rem is a star (split, body, jump); unbounded from m is m - 1 copies and
Rem a plus; bounded is m copies and n - m nested optionals, each of
Rem which is one split in front of a copy.
Def RxRepSize(sb As Number, lo As Number, hi As Number) As Number
    If hi = 0 - 1 Then
        If lo = 0 Then
            sb + 2
        Else
            lo * sb + 1
    Else
        lo * sb + (hi - lo) * (sb + 1)

Rem Concatenation that drops the identity, so (?:) costs nothing and a
Rem chain of optionals ends cleanly. RxSize is unaffected either way,
Rem which is what keeps the arithmetic above honest.
Def RxCatOf(l As RxNode, r As RxNode) As RxNode
    Select Case l
        Case RxNil
            r
        Case Else
            RxCatOf2(l, r)

Def RxCatOf2(l As RxNode, r As RxNode) As RxNode
    Select Case r
        Case RxNil
            l
        Case Else
            RxCat(l, r)

Rem A counted repetition, rewritten into the three primitive ones. Only
Rem ever reached for a shape that is not already primitive, and never
Rem answers the shape it was given, so the emitter below cannot loop.
Def RxExpand(b As RxNode, lo As Number, hi As Number, lz As Boolean) As RxNode
    If hi = 0 - 1 Then
        RxSeqOf(b, lo - 1, RxRep(b, 1, 0 - 1, lz))
    Else
        RxSeqOf(b, lo, RxOptChain(b, hi - lo, lz))

Def RxSeqOf(b As RxNode, k As Number, tail As RxNode) As RxNode
    If k <= 0 Then
        tail
    Else
        RxCatOf(b, RxSeqOf(b, k - 1, tail))

Rem NESTED and not flat: x{2,4} is xx(x(x)?)? and not xx x? x?. For a
Rem body that can match empty the two differ, and the nested form is
Rem the one every other engine agrees with.
Def RxOptChain(b As RxNode, j As Number, lz As Boolean) As RxNode
    If j <= 0 Then
        RxNil()
    Else
        RxRep(RxCatOf(b, RxOptChain(b, j - 1, lz)), 0, 1, lz)

Rem ---- emission -------------------------------------------------------
Rem base is the absolute index the node's first instruction will sit at.

Def RxEmitAt(t As RxNode, base As Number, how As RxOpts) As List Of RxInst
    Select Case t
        Case RxNil
            { }
        Case RxLit(c)
            RxEmitLit(c, how)
        Case RxCls(neg, rs)
            RxEmitCls(neg, rs, how)
        Case RxAny
            { RxIAny(RxDotAll(how)) }
        Case RxBol
            { RxIBol(RxMulti(how)) }
        Case RxEol
            { RxIEol(RxMulti(how)) }
        Case RxWb(nb)
            { RxIWb(nb) }
        Case RxCat(l, r)
            Concat(RxEmitAt(l, base, how), RxEmitAt(r, base + RxSize(l), how))
        Case RxAlt(l, r)
            RxEmitAlt(l, r, base, how)
        Case RxGrp(b, gn)
            Concat(Concat({ RxISave(2 * gn) }, RxEmitAt(b, base + 1, how)), { RxISave(2 * gn + 1) })
        Case RxRep(b, lo, hi, lz)
            RxEmitRep(b, lo, hi, lz, base, how)
        Case Else
            { }

Rem split(left, right), left, jump(past), right. The split ALWAYS
Rem explores its first target first, and priority is list order and
Rem nothing else — which is the whole of how leftmost-first is spelled.
Def RxEmitAlt(l As RxNode, r As RxNode, base As Number, how As RxOpts) As List Of RxInst
    Let sl = RxSize(l)
    Let sr = RxSize(r)
    Concat(Concat(Concat({ RxISplit(base + 1, base + 2 + sl) }, RxEmitAt(l, base + 1, how)), { RxIJmp(base + 2 + sl + sr) }), RxEmitAt(r, base + 2 + sl, how))

Rem The three primitive repetitions, and the general one by rewriting.
Rem A LAZY QUANTIFIER IS THE SAME CODE WITH THE SPLIT'S TWO TARGETS
Rem SWAPPED, and that is the entire difference between greedy and lazy
Rem anywhere in this machine.
Def RxEmitRep(b As RxNode, lo As Number, hi As Number, lz As Boolean, base As Number, how As RxOpts) As List Of RxInst
    If hi = 0 - 1 And lo = 0 Then
        RxEmitStar(b, lz, base, how)
    Else
        If hi = 0 - 1 And lo = 1 Then
            RxEmitPlus(b, lz, base, how)
        Else
            If lo = 0 And hi = 1 Then
                RxEmitOpt(b, lz, base, how)
            Else
                RxEmitAt(RxExpand(b, lo, hi, lz), base, how)

Def RxEmitStar(b As RxNode, lz As Boolean, base As Number, how As RxOpts) As List Of RxInst
    Let sb = RxSize(b)
    Concat(Concat({ RxSplitOf(lz, base + 1, base + 2 + sb) }, RxEmitAt(b, base + 1, how)), { RxIJmp(base) })

Def RxEmitPlus(b As RxNode, lz As Boolean, base As Number, how As RxOpts) As List Of RxInst
    Let sb = RxSize(b)
    Concat(RxEmitAt(b, base, how), { RxSplitOf(lz, base, base + sb + 1) })

Def RxEmitOpt(b As RxNode, lz As Boolean, base As Number, how As RxOpts) As List Of RxInst
    Let sb = RxSize(b)
    Concat({ RxSplitOf(lz, base + 1, base + 1 + sb) }, RxEmitAt(b, base + 1, how))

Rem Greedy prefers the first target, lazy the second.
Def RxSplitOf(lz As Boolean, pref As Number, other As Number) As RxInst
    If lz Then
        RxISplit(other, pref)
    Else
        RxISplit(pref, other)

Rem ---- folding, baked in at compile time ------------------------------
Rem The virtual machine never sees an option: a folded literal compiles
Rem to a two-element class and a folded class carries its own twins, so
Rem the inner loop is one range test either way. A negated folded class
Rem is right by construction — [^a] with folding excludes both a and A,
Rem because the twins go in before the negation is applied.

Def RxEmitLit(c As Number, how As RxOpts) As List Of RxInst
    If RxFold(how) And RxHasCase(c) Then
        { RxICls(False, RxCaseBoth(c)) }
    Else
        { RxIChar(c) }

Def RxHasCase(c As Number) As Boolean
    (c >= rxUpA And c <= rxUpZ) Or (c >= rxLoA And c <= rxLoZ)

Def RxCaseBoth(c As Number) As List Of RxRange
    If c >= rxLoA Then
        { RxRange(c, c), RxRange(c - 32, c - 32) }
    Else
        { RxRange(c, c), RxRange(c + 32, c + 32) }

Def RxEmitCls(neg As Boolean, rs As List Of RxRange, how As RxOpts) As List Of RxInst
    If RxFold(how) Then
        { RxICls(neg, RxFoldRanges(rs)) }
    Else
        { RxICls(neg, rs) }

Def RxFoldRanges(rs As List Of RxRange) As List Of RxRange
    RxFoldGo(rs, rs)

Def RxFoldGo(rs As List Of RxRange, acc As List Of RxRange) As List Of RxRange
    If IsEmpty(rs) Then
        acc
    Else
        RxFoldGo(Rest(rs), Concat(acc, RxCaseTwins(First(rs))))

Def RxCaseTwins(r As RxRange) As List Of RxRange
    Concat(RxTwinDown(r), RxTwinUp(r))

Rem The part of the range inside A-Z, moved to a-z.
Def RxTwinDown(r As RxRange) As List Of RxRange
    Let lo = Max(RxLo(r), rxUpA)
    Let hi = Min(RxHi(r), rxUpZ)
    If lo > hi Then
        { }
    Else
        { RxRange(lo + 32, hi + 32) }

Rem The part of the range inside a-z, moved to A-Z.
Def RxTwinUp(r As RxRange) As List Of RxRange
    Let lo = Max(RxLo(r), rxLoA)
    Let hi = Min(RxHi(r), rxLoZ)
    If lo > hi Then
        { }
    Else
        { RxRange(lo - 32, hi - 32) }

Rem ---- the whole program ----------------------------------------------
Rem save(0), the pattern, save(1), match. Slots 0 and 1 are the whole
Rem match, so the wrapper is what makes RxHitAt and RxHitLen fall out of
Rem the same pass that fills the capture slots.

Def RxBuild(pat As String, t As RxNode, ncap As Number, how As RxOpts) As Result
    Let need = RxSize(t) + 3
    If need > RxMaxCode() Then
        Err("REGEX: THE COMPILED PROGRAM WOULD BE " & Str(need) & " INSTRUCTIONS AND THE LIMIT IS " & Str(RxMaxCode()), 0)
    Else
        Ok(RxProg(pat, ToArray(Concat(Concat({ RxISave(0) }, RxEmitAt(t, 2, how)), { RxISave(1), RxIMatch() })), ncap, how))

Rem ==================================================================
Rem THE VIRTUAL MACHINE
Rem
Rem One pass over Codes(s), k from 1 to Len(s) + 1. Two ordered thread
Rem lists — the one running at k and the one being built for k + 1 —
Rem and per position a visited set over program counters.
Rem
Rem Per position:
Rem
Rem   1. If nothing has matched yet, a new thread is added at the END of
Rem      the current list — LOWEST priority, which is what makes the
Rem      answer leftmost rather than merely a match.
Rem   2. The list is walked IN ORDER. Each thread follows its epsilon
Rem      instructions immediately, adding reached counters to the
Rem      visited set and cutting any branch whose counter has already
Rem      been reached at this position.
Rem   3. A thread reaching match records its slots and CUTS EVERY
Rem      LOWER-PRIORITY THREAD — they can only be worse under
Rem      leftmost-first. Without this the semantics silently become
Rem      leftmost-longest, and nothing else in the machine would say so.
Rem   4. A thread reaching a consuming instruction tests the code unit
Rem      at k; on success it goes onto the next list at pc + 1, on
Rem      failure it dies.
Rem   5. When the next list is empty and a match has been recorded, the
Rem      walk stops early.
Rem
Rem THE WALK OVER POSITIONS AND THE WALK OVER A LIST ARE BOTH SELF-TAIL-
Rem RECURSIVE, and neither recurses into the other, so the mill compiles
Rem each to a loop and a long subject costs no stack. The epsilon
Rem closure is the one place that recurses, and the visited set bounds
Rem it by the program's length.
Rem ==================================================================

Def RxCodeLen(p As RxProg) As Number
    Length(RxCode(p))

Rem ---- the position tests ---------------------------------------------
Rem A line here is one ended by LF and nothing else. CR LF leaves the CR
Rem inside the line, which is the same choice Instr and Split make.

Def RxIsBolAt(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, m As Boolean) As Boolean
    If k = 1 Then
        True
    Else
        m And RxUnitAt(cs, n, k - 1) = rxLf

Def RxIsEolAt(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, m As Boolean) As Boolean
    If k = n + 1 Then
        True
    Else
        m And RxUnitAt(cs, n, k) = rxLf

Rem A boundary is where wordness changes. RxUnitAt answers 0 - 1 off
Rem either end and 0 - 1 is not a word character, so the ends of the
Rem subject fall out with no special case.
Def RxIsWbAt(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number) As Boolean
    RxIsWordCh(RxUnitAt(cs, n, k - 1)) <> RxIsWordCh(RxUnitAt(cs, n, k))

Def RxInSet(c As Number, rs As List Of RxRange) As Boolean
    If IsEmpty(rs) Then
        False
    Else
        If c >= RxLo(First(rs)) And c <= RxHi(First(rs)) Then
            True
        Else
            RxInSet(c, Rest(rs))

Rem ---- the epsilon closure --------------------------------------------
Rem Answers the position's threads in priority order, each parked on a
Rem consuming instruction or on match. Built with Prepend and reversed
Rem once: a List in this runtime is not a cons cell, so every push
Rem copies the spine either way and one Reverse is the cheaper end.

Def RxClose(p As RxProg, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, ts As List Of RxThread) As List Of RxThread
    Reverse(RxAdList(RxCloseGo(p, cs, n, k, ts, RxAdds({ }, Dim(RxCodeLen(p), False)))))

Def RxCloseGo(p As RxProg, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, ts As List Of RxThread, st As RxAdds) As RxAdds
    If IsEmpty(ts) Then
        st
    Else
        RxCloseGo(p, cs, n, k, Rest(ts), RxAddT(p, cs, n, k, st, RxThPc(First(ts)), RxThSlots(First(ts))))

Rem THE VISITED TEST IS WHAT MAKES (a*)* TERMINATE, and it is also what
Rem makes the higher-priority thread win a counter both reach: the first
Rem arrival marks it, and the second is dropped with its slots.
Def RxAddT(p As RxProg, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, st As RxAdds, pc As Number, slots As Array Of Number) As RxAdds
    If pc < 1 Or pc > RxCodeLen(p) Then
        st
    Else
        If Nth(RxAdSeen(st), pc) Then
            st
        Else
            RxAddI(p, cs, n, k, RxAdds(RxAdList(st), SetNth(RxAdSeen(st), pc, True)), pc, slots, Nth(RxCode(p), pc))

Def RxAddI(p As RxProg, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, st As RxAdds, pc As Number, slots As Array Of Number, ins As RxInst) As RxAdds
    Select Case ins
        Case RxISplit(x, y)
            RxAddT(p, cs, n, k, RxAddT(p, cs, n, k, st, x, slots), y, slots)
        Case RxIJmp(t)
            RxAddT(p, cs, n, k, st, t, slots)
        Case RxISave(sl)
            RxAddT(p, cs, n, k, st, pc + 1, SetNth(slots, sl + 1, k))
        Case RxIBol(m)
            RxAddIf(p, cs, n, k, st, pc, slots, RxIsBolAt(cs, n, k, m))
        Case RxIEol(m)
            RxAddIf(p, cs, n, k, st, pc, slots, RxIsEolAt(cs, n, k, m))
        Case RxIWb(nb)
            RxAddIf(p, cs, n, k, st, pc, slots, RxIsWbAt(cs, n, k) <> nb)
        Case Else
            RxAdds(Prepend(RxThread(pc, slots), RxAdList(st)), RxAdSeen(st))

Rem An assertion consumes nothing: it either lets the thread through to
Rem the next instruction or ends it.
Def RxAddIf(p As RxProg, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, st As RxAdds, pc As Number, slots As Array Of Number, held As Boolean) As RxAdds
    If held Then
        RxAddT(p, cs, n, k, st, pc + 1, slots)
    Else
        st

Rem ---- the consuming step ---------------------------------------------

Def RxEats(p As RxProg, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, pc As Number) As Boolean
    If k > n Then
        False
    Else
        RxEatsI(Nth(RxCode(p), pc), Nth(cs, k))

Def RxEatsI(ins As RxInst, c As Number) As Boolean
    Select Case ins
        Case RxIChar(cc)
            c = cc
        Case RxICls(neg, rs)
            RxInSet(c, rs) <> neg
        Case RxIAny(all)
            all Or c <> rxLf
        Case Else
            False

Def RxIsMatchAt(p As RxProg, pc As Number) As Boolean
    Select Case Nth(RxCode(p), pc)
        Case RxIMatch
            True
        Case Else
            False

Rem Walks the position's threads in priority order. Reaching match ends
Rem the walk with that thread's slots: every thread still behind it is
Rem lower priority and cannot improve on it.
Def RxStepGo(p As RxProg, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, cl As List Of RxThread, st As RxStep) As RxStep
    If IsEmpty(cl) Then
        st
    Else
        Let th = First(cl)
        Let pc = RxThPc(th)
        If pc < 1 Or pc > RxCodeLen(p) Then
            RxStepGo(p, cs, n, k, Rest(cl), st)
        Else
            If RxIsMatchAt(p, pc) Then
                RxStep(RxStPend(st), RxThSlots(th))
            Else
                If RxEats(p, cs, n, k, pc) Then
                    RxStepGo(p, cs, n, k, Rest(cl), RxStep(Prepend(RxThread(pc + 1, RxThSlots(th)), RxStPend(st)), RxStBest(st)))
                Else
                    RxStepGo(p, cs, n, k, Rest(cl), st)

Rem ---- the walk over positions ----------------------------------------
Rem best is the slot array of the best match so far. Slot 1 is where the
Rem whole match started, and a start is always at least 1, so 0 there
Rem means "nothing has matched yet" — a sentinel that no real answer can
Rem collide with, and the only one in the machine.

Def RxBlank(p As RxProg) As Array Of Number
    Dim(2 * RxNCap(p) + 2, 0)

Def RxGo(p As RxProg, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, pend As List Of RxThread, best As Array Of Number, from As Number, anchored As Boolean) As Array Of Number
    If k > n + 1 Then
        best
    Else
        Let seed = Nth(best, 1) = 0 And (Not anchored Or k = from)
        If IsEmpty(pend) And Not seed Then
            best
        Else
            Let st = RxStepGo(p, cs, n, k, RxClose(p, cs, n, k, RxSeeded(p, pend, seed)), RxStep({ }, best))
            RxGo(p, cs, n, k + 1, Reverse(RxStPend(st)), RxStBest(st), from, anchored)

Rem The new thread goes at the END of the list, which is what makes an
Rem earlier start beat a later one at every position.
Def RxSeeded(p As RxProg, pend As List Of RxThread, seed As Boolean) As List Of RxThread
    If seed Then
        Concat(pend, { RxThread(1, RxBlank(p)) })
    Else
        pend

Rem ---- from slots to an answer ----------------------------------------

Def RxRunIn(p As RxProg, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, from As Number, anchored As Boolean) As Array Of Number
    RxGo(p, cs, n, RxFromOf(from), { }, RxBlank(p), RxFromOf(from), anchored)

Rem A start below 1 is clamped to 1 and a fractional one is floored.
Rem THIS IS A CONTRACT AND NOT A MASK: it is stated here, stated on the
Rem docs page, and the value it produces is the value the caller meant.
Rem A start past Len(s) + 1 needs no clamp — the walk ends at once and
Rem answers None, which is a true statement: nothing starts there.
Def RxFromOf(from As Number) As Number
    Max(1, Floor(from))

Def RxHitFrom(p As RxProg, s As String, best As Array Of Number) As RxHit
    RxHit(Nth(best, 1), Nth(best, 2) - Nth(best, 1), Mid(s, Nth(best, 1), Nth(best, 2) - Nth(best, 1)), RxCapsOf(p, s, best, 1, { }))

Def RxHitOf(p As RxProg, s As String, best As Array Of Number) As Option
    If Nth(best, 1) = 0 Then
        None()
    Else
        Some(RxHitFrom(p, s, best))

Rem Exactly RxCount(p) entries, always, in group order. A hit never
Rem carries a short list, so a caller counting them is counting groups.
Def RxCapsOf(p As RxProg, s As String, best As Array Of Number, gn As Number, acc As List Of RxCap) As List Of RxCap
    If gn > RxNCap(p) Then
        Reverse(acc)
    Else
        RxCapsOf(p, s, best, gn + 1, Prepend(RxCapFor(s, best, gn), acc))

Def RxCapFor(s As String, best As Array Of Number, gn As Number) As RxCap
    Let a = Nth(best, 2 * gn + 1)
    Let b = Nth(best, 2 * gn + 2)
    If a = 0 Or b = 0 Then
        RxUnset()
    Else
        RxGot(a, Mid(s, a, b - a))

Rem ==================================================================
Rem THE WORD SURFACE
Rem
Rem Every word below takes a COMPILED PROGRAM, which can only have come
Rem from an Ok. There is no argument left that can be wrong, which is
Rem what makes all of them total without a Result between them and the
Rem caller.
Rem ==================================================================

Rem ---- asking ---------------------------------------------------------

Def RxTest(p As RxProg, s As String) As Boolean
    Nth(RxRunIn(p, Codes(s), Len(s), 1, False), 1) <> 0

Rem RxFind TAKES NO OFFSET AT ALL, and that is the point of its existing
Rem beside RxFindFrom: the common call has no argument that can be out
Rem of range, so the clamp is a rule about the one word that needs it
Rem rather than a rule about the surface.
Def RxFind(p As RxProg, s As String) As Option
    RxHitOf(p, s, RxRunIn(p, Codes(s), Len(s), 1, False))

Def RxFindFrom(p As RxProg, s As String, from As Number) As Option
    RxHitOf(p, s, RxRunIn(p, Codes(s), Len(s), from, False))

Rem Anchored at exactly one offset: it either starts there or nowhere.
Def RxMatchAt(p As RxProg, s As String, at As Number) As Option
    RxHitOf(p, s, RxRunIn(p, Codes(s), Len(s), at, True))

Rem ---- every match ----------------------------------------------------
Rem ONE WALK, SHARED. RxFindAll, RxReplace, RxReplaceFirst,
Rem RxReplaceWith and RxSplit all come through here, so the empty-match
Rem rule below is implemented once. Implemented three times it would
Rem agree twice.
Rem
Rem THE EMPTY-MATCH RULE. A pattern that can match empty would otherwise
Rem make every all-matches word non-terminating:
Rem
Rem   * after a match of length 0 at k, the next search starts at k + 1;
Rem   * after a match of length > 0 ending at k, the next search starts
Rem     at k + 1 as well, so matches never overlap.
Rem
Rem The number of matches over a subject of length n is therefore at
Rem most n + 1, always. Worked, because it is the one result callers
Rem find surprising — RxFindAll of a* over "baa" is THREE hits:
Rem
Rem   1. search at 1: "" (the b is not an a), length 0, so next is 2
Rem   2. search at 2: "aa", length 2, ending at 3, so next is 4
Rem   3. search at 4: "" at Len(s) + 1, past the end, so next is 5,
Rem      which stops the walk

Def RxFindAll(p As RxProg, s As String) As List Of RxHit
    RxWalk(p, s, Codes(s), Len(s), 1, { })

Def RxWalk(p As RxProg, s As String, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, acc As List Of RxHit) As List Of RxHit
    If k > n + 1 Then
        Reverse(acc)
    Else
        Let best = RxGo(p, cs, n, k, { }, RxBlank(p), k, False)
        If Nth(best, 1) = 0 Then
            Reverse(acc)
        Else
            Let h = RxHitFrom(p, s, best)
            RxWalk(p, s, cs, n, RxNextStart(h), Prepend(h, acc))

Def RxNextStart(h As RxHit) As Number
    If RxHitLen(h) = 0 Then
        RxHitAt(h) + 1
    Else
        RxHitAt(h) + RxHitLen(h)

Rem ---- reading a hit --------------------------------------------------

Rem Group 0 is the whole match, so RxGroup and a $0 in a template agree.
Rem A group that does not exist and a group that did not participate are
Rem both None; RxCount answers how many exist if the caller needs to
Rem tell those two apart.
Def RxGroup(h As RxHit, gn As Number) As Option
    If gn = 0 Then
        Some(RxHitText(h))
    Else
        If gn < 1 Or gn > Length(RxHitCaps(h)) Then
            None()
        Else
            RxCapOpt(Nth(RxHitCaps(h), gn))

Def RxCapOpt(c As RxCap) As Option
    Select Case c
        Case RxGot(a, t)
            Some(t)
        Case Else
            None()

Def RxGroupOr(h As RxHit, gn As Number, dflt As String) As String
    Select Case RxGroup(h, gn)
        Case Some(t)
            t
        Case Else
            dflt

Rem ---- asking about the program ---------------------------------------

Def RxSource(p As RxProg) As String
    RxSrc(p)

Def RxCount(p As RxProg) As Number
    RxNCap(p)

Rem ---- rewriting ------------------------------------------------------
Rem Within a replacement, $0 is the whole match and $1 to $9 are groups;
Rem $$ is a literal $; a $ followed by anything else is a literal $.
Rem A REFERENCE TO AN UNSET OR NONEXISTENT GROUP EXPANDS TO THE EMPTY
Rem STRING. The alternative is to make RxReplace answer a Result, so
Rem every caller matches on a failure mode that only fires when a group
Rem legitimately did not participate — a worse trade, and RxReplaceWith
Rem is the escape hatch for anything a template cannot say.

Def RxReplace(p As RxProg, s As String, rep As String) As String
    RxRepGo(s, rep, RxFindAll(p, s), 1, "")

Def RxRepGo(s As String, rep As String, hs As List Of RxHit, at As Number, acc As String) As String
    If IsEmpty(hs) Then
        acc & Mid(s, at, Len(s) - at + 1)
    Else
        Let h = First(hs)
        RxRepGo(s, rep, Rest(hs), RxHitAt(h) + RxHitLen(h), acc & Mid(s, at, RxHitAt(h) - at) & RxExpandTpl(rep, h))

Def RxReplaceFirst(p As RxProg, s As String, rep As String) As String
    Select Case RxFind(p, s)
        Case Some(h)
            Mid(s, 1, RxHitAt(h) - 1) & RxExpandTpl(rep, h) & Mid(s, RxHitAt(h) + RxHitLen(h), Len(s))
        Case Else
            s

Def RxReplaceWith(p As RxProg, s As String, f As [ RxHit -- String ]) As String
    RxRepWGo(s, f, RxFindAll(p, s), 1, "")

Def RxRepWGo(s As String, f As [ RxHit -- String ], hs As List Of RxHit, at As Number, acc As String) As String
    If IsEmpty(hs) Then
        acc & Mid(s, at, Len(s) - at + 1)
    Else
        Let h = First(hs)
        RxRepWGo(s, f, Rest(hs), RxHitAt(h) + RxHitLen(h), acc & Mid(s, at, RxHitAt(h) - at) & Call(f, h))

Def RxExpandTpl(rep As String, h As RxHit) As String
    RxTplGo(rep, Codes(rep), Len(rep), h, 1, "")

Def RxTplGo(rep As String, rc As Array Of Number, m As Number, h As RxHit, i As Number, acc As String) As String
    If i > m Then
        acc
    Else
        Let c = Nth(rc, i)
        If c <> rxDollar Then
            RxTplGo(rep, rc, m, h, i + 1, acc & Mid(rep, i, 1))
        Else
            Let c2 = RxUnitAt(rc, m, i + 1)
            If c2 = rxDollar Then
                RxTplGo(rep, rc, m, h, i + 2, acc & "$")
            Else
                If RxIsDigitC(c2) Then
                    RxTplGo(rep, rc, m, h, i + 2, acc & RxGroupOr(h, c2 - rxZero, ""))
                Else
                    RxTplGo(rep, rc, m, h, i + 1, acc & "$")

Rem ---- splitting ------------------------------------------------------
Rem The pieces between matches, in order, including leading and trailing
Rem empty ones — so a pattern matching the whole subject gives two empty
Rem pieces and not none. A PATTERN WITH CAPTURING GROUPS DOES NOT EMIT
Rem THEM INTO THE RESULT: Python always does and JavaScript sometimes
Rem does, and both make the return type "sometimes separators, sometimes
Rem not". RxFindAll is the word for callers who want the separators.

Def RxSplit(p As RxProg, s As String) As List Of String
    RxSplitGo(s, RxFindAll(p, s), 1, { })

Def RxSplitGo(s As String, hs As List Of RxHit, at As Number, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(hs) Then
        Reverse(Prepend(Mid(s, at, Len(s) - at + 1), acc))
    Else
        Let h = First(hs)
        RxSplitGo(s, Rest(hs), RxHitAt(h) + RxHitLen(h), Prepend(Mid(s, at, RxHitAt(h) - at), acc))

Rem ---- escaping -------------------------------------------------------
Rem s escaped so that it matches itself and nothing else. The text is
Rem taken from the subject with Mid rather than rebuilt from its code,
Rem so a character outside ASCII passes through untouched; a NUL and the
Rem other controls are written as \xHH, which is why the result is safe
Rem to paste into a pattern typed at a prompt.

Def RxQuote(s As String) As String
    RxQuoteGo(s, Codes(s), Len(s), 1, "")

Def RxQuoteGo(s As String, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, k As Number, acc As String) As String
    If k > n Then
        acc
    Else
        RxQuoteGo(s, cs, n, k + 1, acc & RxQuoteOne(s, Nth(cs, k), k))

Def RxQuoteOne(s As String, c As Number, k As Number) As String
    If RxIsMeta(c) Then
        RxBs() & Mid(s, k, 1)
    Else
        If c < 32 Or c = 127 Then
            RxBs() & "x" & RxHex2(c)
        Else
            Mid(s, k, 1)

Def RxHex2(c As Number) As String
    RxHexDigit(Floor(c / 16)) & RxHexDigit(c - 16 * Floor(c / 16))

Def RxHexDigit(v As Number) As String
    Mid("0123456789ABCDEF", v + 1, 1)

Rem ---- the compiled program, as printable lines -----------------------
Rem It earns its place twice: it is how the docs page shows what
Rem "compiled to a program" means, and it is how a disagreeing test cell
Rem gets diagnosed. It answers lines; it does not print them.

Def RxDisasm(p As RxProg) As List Of String
    RxDisGo(p, 1, { })

Def RxDisGo(p As RxProg, i As Number, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If i > RxCodeLen(p) Then
        Reverse(acc)
    Else
        RxDisGo(p, i + 1, Prepend(RxPad(Str(i), 4) & "  " & RxShowI(Nth(RxCode(p), i)), acc))

Def RxPad(s As String, w As Number) As String
    If Len(s) >= w Then
        s
    Else
        RxPad(" " & s, w)

Def RxShowI(ins As RxInst) As String
    Select Case ins
        Case RxIChar(c)
            "CHAR   " & RxShowCode(c)
        Case RxICls(neg, rs)
            RxClsWord(neg) & RxShowRs(rs)
        Case RxIAny(all)
            RxAnyWord(all)
        Case RxISplit(x, y)
            "SPLIT  " & Str(x) & ", " & Str(y)
        Case RxIJmp(t)
            "JMP    " & Str(t)
        Case RxISave(sl)
            "SAVE   " & Str(sl)
        Case RxIBol(m)
            RxBolWord(m)
        Case RxIEol(m)
            RxEolWord(m)
        Case RxIWb(nb)
            RxWbWord(nb)
        Case Else
            "MATCH"

Def RxClsWord(neg As Boolean) As String
    If neg Then
        "NCLASS "
    Else
        "CLASS  "

Def RxAnyWord(all As Boolean) As String
    If all Then
        "ANY    (dot-all)"
    Else
        "ANY    (not a newline)"

Def RxBolWord(m As Boolean) As String
    If m Then
        "BOL    (line)"
    Else
        "BOL"

Def RxEolWord(m As Boolean) As String
    If m Then
        "EOL    (line)"
    Else
        "EOL"

Def RxWbWord(nb As Boolean) As String
    If nb Then
        "NWORDB"
    Else
        "WORDB"

Rem A code, and its character where that character can be shown. This is
Rem the machine's one use of FromCodes, and it is deliberate: Chr would
Rem answer the empty string for a NUL and the line would lie.
Def RxShowCode(c As Number) As String
    If c >= 32 And c <= 126 Then
        Str(c) & " " & FromCodes({ c })
    Else
        Str(c)

Def RxShowRs(rs As List Of RxRange) As String
    If IsEmpty(rs) Then
        ""
    Else
        If IsEmpty(Rest(rs)) Then
            RxShowR(First(rs))
        Else
            RxShowR(First(rs)) & " " & RxShowRs(Rest(rs))

Def RxShowR(r As RxRange) As String
    If RxLo(r) = RxHi(r) Then
        Str(RxLo(r))
    Else
        Str(RxLo(r)) & "-" & Str(RxHi(r))
